From: The pixel5-ubuntu contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ipv4: treat RTA_GATEWAY 0.0.0.0 as "no gateway"

NetworkManager 1.46 adds IPv4 link routes with an explicit RTA_GATEWAY of
0.0.0.0. This 4.19 tree (with the nexthop gateway-family backports) sets
fc_gw_family = AF_INET for any RTA_GATEWAY, so fib_check_nh_v4_gw() looks
up 0.0.0.0 and fails with -ENETUNREACH "Nexthop has invalid gateway". The
prefix route for every NM-managed interface (usb0, later wlan0) is never
added. Only mark a gateway when it is non-zero, as newer kernels do.

pixel5-ubuntu Test 17 (docs/log.md).
---
diff --git a/net/ipv4/fib_frontend.c b/net/ipv4/fib_frontend.c
index 6950b55df..b0012f3d6 100644
--- a/net/ipv4/fib_frontend.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/fib_frontend.c
@@ -755,8 +755,9 @@ static int rtm_to_fib_config(struct net *net, struct sk_buff *skb,
 			break;
 		case RTA_GATEWAY:
 			has_gw = true;
-			cfg->fc_gw_family = AF_INET;
 			cfg->fc_gw4 = nla_get_be32(attr);
+			if (cfg->fc_gw4)
+				cfg->fc_gw_family = AF_INET;
 			break;
 		case RTA_VIA:
 			has_via = true;
